    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636-a1">

                <pb facs="0719" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg639"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beck to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of August 12, 1902, in which you ask me to enforce the due
                    observance of neutrality obligations by preventing the shipment of arms and
                    ammunition to Haiti.</p>
                <p>At the present this Department has no knowledge of any intended shipment. Should
                    it receive such information it will promptly invoke the action of the courts to
                    prevent such shipments.</p>
                <p>If you deem the matter of sufficient importance, and desire it, I will cause
                    instructions to be issued to the United States attorneys for the districts in
                    which there are ports of entry.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jas. M. Beck</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Attorney-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
